{
  "description": "Generic instrument generator — GENERATE { subject, context } picks one learning instrument for a subject and writes its roster. It lists the installed behaviors under `scope` (optionally narrowed to the `instruments` allow-list), keeps those whose trait listens for ROSTER_LOADED (an instrument that takes its roster at runtime), asks the model to CHOOSE one, then to FILL a roster whose fields are exactly that instrument's ROSTER_LOADED payload; the tool loop checks the roster against those declared fields before it is accepted. GENERATED { behavior, mode, roster } carries the instrument, its mode (the behavior's name, the matchMode a lab router uses) and the roster as JSON, ready to send as that instrument's ROSTER_LOADED. It never writes a program: when no instrument in scope fits or the roster cannot be filled, it emits GENERATE_FAILED { error }. The instrument list is read once and kept for later requests.",
